("h1", "Outlook for 2026"),
("p", "The Group entered 2026 with a record order backlog of £97.3m and good momentum in all three segments. The Board expects Group revenue for 2026 of between £200m and £210m, including about ten months of contribution from Brightwater Acoustics."),
("p", "The Board expects the operating margin to improve further in 2026, towards 15.5%, as Harbourline continues to grow and the Tidewatch T5 line reaches full efficiency. This guidance assumes exchange rates similar to those at the start of the year."),
("h2", "Segment expectations"),
("p", "For Tidewatch buoys, the full-year effect of the T5 and steady demand from offshore wind farms are expected to support mid-single-digit growth. Demand for the T3 is expected to be flat as some customers move to the T5."),
("p", "For Kestrel sonar, the order backlog includes the Baltic Sea cable survey programme, and the Group expects growth of around 10%, with Kestrel Deep entering field trials in the second half of the year."),
("p", "For Harbourline software, the Group expects annual recurring revenue to rise by more than 25%, helped by the Channel Depth Assurance module and by customers who buy the T5."),
("h2", "Investment"),
("p", "Capital expenditure in 2026 is expected to be between £12m and £14m, lower than in 2025 now that the T5 line is complete. Research and development spending is expected to remain at around 9% of revenue."),
("h2", "Risks to the outlook"),
("p", "The main risks to this outlook are delays to large offshore wind projects, which could shift Kestrel and Tidewatch deliveries into 2027, and further strengthening of sterling. The Board will update the market in its first-half trading statement, planned for July 2026."),
("p", "Overall, the Board is confident that the Group is on track to deliver the Course 2028 targets of £260m revenue and a 17% operating margin."),
